cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "Range Chart Analyzer: LLM-based extraction of stratigraphic range charts into structured data"
abstract: >-
  Range Chart Analyzer reads a published stratigraphic range chart, columnar
  section, abundance diagram, zonation chart, phylogenetic tree or occurrence
  matrix, and extracts it into structured, editable, standards-conformant
  data. It uses a vision language model, records a full evidence chain for
  every extraction, and exports Darwin Core, PBDB and ICS tables alongside
  CSV, TSV, JSON and XLSX.
type: software
version: 0.1.4
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: "See LICENSE. The software inherits the upstream RLPE-Radiolarian-Plate-Extractor terms and is provided for research and educational use only. Data exported by the tool is released under CC0 1.0."
repository-code: "https://github.com/syxscott/Range-chart-Analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/syxscott/Range-chart-Analyzer"
keywords:
  - palaeontology
  - micropalaeontology
  - biostratigraphy
  - range chart
  - radiolarians
  - conodonts
  - Darwin Core
  - Paleobiology Database
  - ICS chronostratigraphy
  - vision language model
